WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590 line:90%
We want to get the latest from

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.360 line:90%
Dr. Tom Engels be director

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.320 line:90%
of the Center for Health

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.360 line:90%
Security at Johns Hopkins

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.730 line:90%
University doctor I want

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.160 line:90%
to start with some more numbers

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.510 line:90%
put him up on the screen more

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.360 line:90%
than 83,000 people are now

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.990 line:90%
hospitalized in this country.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.860 line:90%
That's a record high over 16,000

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.490 line:90%
are in ICUs and more than 5,000

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.220 line:90%
are on ventilators why are we

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.400 line:90%
seeing this new spike right now

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.420 line:90%
and how close are we

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.190 line:90%
to overwhelming our health care

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:32.990 line:90%
system.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.160 line:90%
Well good morning Chris.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.960 line:90%
Thanks for having me

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.630 line:90%
on your show we are seeing this

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:44.220 line:90%
new spike because of the gradual

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.360 line:90%
accumulation of choices

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.470 line:90%
and policies over the last

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.720 line:90%
couple of months this virus has

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.310 line:90%
the ability to spread

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.070 line:90%
exponentially meaning more

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.820 line:90%
and more rapidly if we let it.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.600 line:90%
And unlike the springtime when

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.850 line:90%
the country really was acting

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.770 line:90%
kind of with common purpose

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.060 line:90%
around March and April

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.140 line:90%
at the start of this pandemic

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.470 line:90%
and where the virus was located

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.220 line:90%
in comparatively fewer Cape

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.620 line:90%
places the epidemic now is

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.630 line:90%
surging in almost every state

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.010 line:90%
in the country with the Midwest

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.030 line:90%
and the Mountain West really

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.760 line:90%
being out really in front

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.440 line:90%
in terms of rapidly accelerating

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.620 line:90%
numbers of cases.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:21.960 line:90%
So it's not it's not confined

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.580 line:90%
to a few places it's really

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.970 line:90%
spread across the country.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.040 line:90%
It's not just in big cities

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.930 line:90%
but it's in rural locations

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.150 line:90%
small towns and so that is

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.950 line:90%
adding up to record numbers

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.550 line:90%
of hospitalizations.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.580 line:90%
And as you said the pressure

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.080 line:90%
on hospitals is the highest

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.460 line:90%
it's been since the beginning

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.530 line:90%
of the pandemic with about 1,000

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.760 line:90%
hospitals reporting this week

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.620 line:90%
that they are critically short

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.940 line:90%
on health care workers or will

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.410 line:90%
be very soon and that number

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.890 line:90%
will grow this week.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.440 line:90%
So it's a very very serious

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.730 line:90%
moment for the country in terms

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:55.110 line:90%
of this pandemic at least 37

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.660 line:90%
states are now requiring people

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.430 line:90%
to wear masks in public

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.010 line:90%
but the debate over masks

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.890 line:90%
and partial or total closures

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.800 line:90%
shutdowns is continuing here is

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.270 line:90%
South Dakota Governor Christie

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.330 line:90%
no I'm not in favor of mandating

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.490 line:90%
mask wearing I don't believe

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.080 line:90%
that I have the authority

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.090 line:90%
to mandate that and that people

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.200 line:90%
can use their own personal

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.280 line:90%
responsibility to make

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.390 line:90%
a decision when it comes

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:25.480 line:90%
to masks what about the argument

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.490 line:90%
that government can recommend

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.080 line:90%
but it shouldn't be ordering

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:34.000 line:90%
people what to do or not to do

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.890 line:90%
well we trust government to do

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.520 line:90%
things to keep us safe.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.130 line:90%
So we trust government to set

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.750 line:90%
speed limits in neighborhoods

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.820 line:90%
so we don't drive too fast

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.340 line:90%
and risk injuring or killing

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.240 line:90%
kids or playing in the street

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.240 line:90%
and a neighborhood so I think

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.220 line:90%
that would be the analogy I

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.020 line:90%
would think of here.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.330 line:90%
I think there are some times

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.320 line:90%
when it's really important

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.510 line:90%
for government to set the rules

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.420 line:90%
and to ask people to follow

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.220 line:90%
them.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.287 line:90%
And I think this is one of those

00:02:59.287 --> 00:03:01.990 line:90%
times if 37 states can set mask

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.220 line:90%
mandates then the rest

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.300 line:90%
of the states can set mask

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.750 line:90%
mandates as well and they should

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.010 line:90%
let me ask you about another

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.290 line:90%
aspect of this particular debate

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.110 line:90%
New York City just shut down its

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:16.600 line:90%
public schools school system

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.700 line:90%
forcing more than one million

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.330 line:90%
students to stay at home.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.910 line:90%
But there is some growing

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.490 line:90%
evidence that in fact schools

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.200 line:90%
are not major spreaders

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.270 line:90%
of the disease here is CDC

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.040 line:90%
director Dr. Robert Redfield

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.740 line:90%
this week the truth is for kids

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.120 line:90%
K through 12 one of the safest

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.790 line:90%
place they can be from

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.010 line:90%
our perspective is to remain

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:42.400 line:90%
in school doctor

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.440 line:90%
what's the science are kids

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:49.260 line:90%
safer staying in school so it

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.400 line:90%
does look like at the K through

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.600 line:90%
level of school that kids are

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.490 line:90%
both at certainly at lower risk

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:59.340 line:90%
of serious disease and probably

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.300 line:90%
because of the way school

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.460 line:90%
happens smaller groups of kids

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.470 line:90%
not mixing together no large

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:07.800 line:90%
assemblies that they are safer

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.330 line:90%
than high schools

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.460 line:90%
or universities for example we

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.570 line:90%
haven't had reports of major

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.370 line:90%
outbreaks

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:15.750 line:90%
driving transmission

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.390 line:90%
in communities but on the other

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.190 line:90%
hand,

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.100 line:90%
we are not systematically enough

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.120 line:90%
collecting data around

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.070 line:90%
the country right now

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.850 line:90%
and the schools that have made

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.050 line:90%
mitigation measures have been

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.120 line:90%
able to decrease classroom

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.820 line:90%
density have been able to have

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.210 line:90%
kids wear masks and assemblies

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.280 line:90%
change pickup and drop off those

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.560 line:90%
schools we think are doing

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.300 line:90%
better and are creating safer

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.063 line:90%
environments but not all schools

00:04:44.063 --> 00:04:45.030 line:90%
have been able to do that not

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:45.830 line:90%
all schools have had

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.040 line:90%
the resources to put mitigation

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.050 line:90%
measures in place so I do think

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.280 line:90%
it's hard to have universal

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.080 line:90%
rules I don't think we can go

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.940 line:90%
that far but in places where

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:54.840 line:90%
they've put mitigation

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.460 line:90%
procedures in place

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.530 line:90%
and community transmission

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.580 line:90%
in that particular school

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.780 line:90%
district is relatively low I do

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:02.580 line:90%
think those

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:03.870 line:90%
are safer environments

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.520 line:90%
the problem is that now we are

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.110 line:90%
seeing transmission levels

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.820 line:90%
across the country that are

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.930 line:90%
higher than they've ever been

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:10.770 line:90%
since the start of this

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.570 line:90%
pandemic.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:12.540 line:90%
So we are kind of entering

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.250 line:90%
in uncharted territory in many

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.800 line:90%
places which have enormous rates

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:17.940 line:90%
of spread.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:18.940 line:90%
So we haven't seen those rates

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:19.800 line:90%
of spread in other parts

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:20.380 line:90%
of the world.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.347 line:90%
So we don't really have those

00:05:21.347 --> 00:05:22.850 line:90%
places to learn from.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:23.850 line:90%
And I think we have to be very

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.890 line:90%
cautious about about making

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.000 line:90%
judgments about safety

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.620 line:90%
in schools when the rate gets

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:32.640 line:90%
so high in communities and then

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.290 line:90%
there is Thanksgiving we are

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.450 line:90%
seeing already airports with

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:39.360 line:90%
long lines of people waiting

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.480 line:90%
on line going through security

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.090 line:90%
getting on planes should people

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.090 line:90%
travel for Thanksgiving or not

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.400 line:90%
and if they're bound to anyway

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.680 line:90%
what can they do to minimize

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:52.480 line:90%
their risk.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.020 line:90%
So I would recommend that people

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.420 line:90%
do not travel on Thanksgiving

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.860 line:90%
for this particular holiday I

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.060 line:90%
think if you look at the map

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.170 line:90%
of spread across the country.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.840 line:90%
You can see the risk is very

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:10.010 line:90%
visible and moving through

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:14.090 line:90%
airports or travel hubs I think

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.290 line:90%
that will increase

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:16.440 line:90%
people's risk.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.660 line:90%
But even if they're driving from

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.630 line:90%
point to point unfortunately we

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.760 line:90%
don't know if we're infected

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.380 line:90%
when we walk into a gathering

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.710 line:90%
CDC came out with data.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.620 line:90%
This week that said that more

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.510 line:90%
than 50% of infections that are

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:31.250 line:90%
happening are caused by people

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.000 line:90%
with no symptoms.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:33.800 line:90%
So I think the message

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.960 line:90%
for everyone is you can't assume

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:37.580 line:90%
that you don't have the virus

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.510 line:90%
and you can't assume that

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:40.100 line:90%
the people whose home

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.270 line:90%
you're about to enter don't have

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:42.470 line:90%
the virus at this point

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:44.070 line:90%
in our pandemic.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.500 line:90%
And so we really should

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.910 line:90%
discourage traveling and kind

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:47.810 line:90%
of stick with our nuclear

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.190 line:90%
families the people that we live

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:52.070 line:90%
with if you are going to travel

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:52.970 line:90%
to someone else's home

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.950 line:90%
for Thanksgiving then

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.270 line:90%
if possible you should spend

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.100 line:90%
as much time outdoors when

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.510 line:90%
you're together in some places

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:00.770 line:90%
that may be possible with

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.690 line:90%
the weather other places not

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:03.950 line:90%
people should be wearing masks

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.690 line:90%
indoors when they're together

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:06.620 line:90%
and only removing them when

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.740 line:90%
they're eating.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.080 line:90%
We should probably keep meals

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.970 line:90%
short and spend more time with

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.480 line:90%
masks on.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.700 line:90%
And the smaller the gatherings

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.300 line:90%
the better but in general,

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.490 line:90%
I would recommend against it I

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.020 line:90%
love being with my family

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.850 line:90%
on Thanksgiving but this year

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:20.870 line:90%
we're staying home just

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:26.030 line:90%
our nuclear family but Dr. Scott

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:27.980 line:90%
Atlas who is one of President

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.680 line:90%
Trump's top COVID 19 officials

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.890 line:90%
gave very different advice this

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:33.690 line:90%
week.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:35.900 line:90%
Take a look this kind

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:37.040 line:90%
of isolation is one

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.450 line:90%
of the unspoken tragedies

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.400 line:90%
of the elderly who are now being

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.750 line:90%
told don't see your family

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.770 line:90%
at Thanksgiving for many people,

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.380 line:90%
this is their final Thanksgiving

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.120 line:90%
believe it or not what are we

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.550 line:90%
doing here straight out should

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.190 line:90%
people listen to Doctor outlets

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:56.720 line:90%
or not you know I don't think

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:57.520 line:90%
so.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:59.850 line:90%
I think there there are a number

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.850 line:90%
of officials from the US

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.740 line:90%
government who have 30 years

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:06.540 line:90%
of experience preparing

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.050 line:90%
for and responding to infectious

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.520 line:90%
disease outbreaks including Dr.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.620 line:90%
Phil g and I think their advice

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.000 line:90%
has been very clear CDC is

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.470 line:90%
advice is very clear CDC whose

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.930 line:90%
job is to try to prevent

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.850 line:90%
the spread of outbreaks.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.030 line:90%
I think I don't know Dr. Atlas

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:25.440 line:90%
but his background is quite

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.470 line:90%
different.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:29.310 line:90%
And I think we should stick with

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.410 line:90%
the scientists who've led us

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.429 line:90%
through past outbreaks I've got

00:08:35.429 --> 00:08:36.897 line:90%
two questions I want to squeeze

00:08:36.897 --> 00:08:37.830 line:90%
in here so I'm going to need

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.270 line:90%
quick answers from you first

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.580 line:90%
of all, there is some good news

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.039 line:90%
and that of course, is the fact

00:08:43.039 --> 00:08:44.670 line:90%
that looks like that we have not

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.220 line:90%
one but two vaccines as part

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.840 line:90%
of Operation Warp Speed that are

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.140 line:90%
on the way Pfizer on Friday

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.910 line:90%
applied for emergency use

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.310 line:90%
authorization assuming that

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.320 line:90%
they're approved by the FDA how

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:01.230 line:90%
confident should Americans be

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:04.870 line:90%
about taking these vaccines.

